// The rock under the ground (docs/04-architecture.md, D42): granite,
// limestone, chalk or sandstone, a region each. Drawn only on worlds made
// by the generator's version 2 on (D24); a world made by the first keeps
// none. Placeholder values, tuned by eye on the overview of a 6 km world.
//
// region_m:       side of the coarse grid's cells, in metres: a region's
//                 usual breadth. A real region is 10 to 100 km; the game
//                 compresses it five to fifty times (2 km). A 6 km world
//                 shows three to six patches of two to four rocks.
// border_cell_m:  cell of the noise that shifts the borders, in metres:
//                 the size of their bends.
// border_shift_m: how far that noise shifts a border at most, each way, in
//                 metres. Under region_m.
// weights:        how often each rock is a region's, against the others.
//                 Every rock must appear; 0 leaves it out.
(
    region_m: 2000,
    border_cell_m: 100,
    border_shift_m: 150,
    weights: {
        granite: 30,
        limestone: 30,
        chalk: 20,
        sandstone: 20,
    },
)
